# Testing Guidelines

## Testing Framework

This project uses Jest with jest-expo preset for testing:

### Test Structure

- **Unit tests**: Test individual functions and components
- **Integration tests**: Test component interactions
- **E2E tests**: Test complete user flows (when applicable)
- **Test files**: Use `.test.ts` or `.test.tsx` extensions

### Component Testing

- **Test component rendering** with proper props
- **Test user interactions** (press, scroll, input)
- **Test error states** and loading states
- **Test accessibility** features
- **Mock external dependencies** appropriately

### Hook Testing

- **Test custom hooks** with `@testing-library/react-hooks`
- **Test hook state changes** and side effects
- **Test error handling** in hooks
- **Test cleanup** functions

### Example Usage

```typescript
import { render, screen, fireEvent } from "@testing-library/react-native";
import { NoteItem } from "../NoteItem";

describe("NoteItem", () => {
  const mockNote = {
    id: "1",
    title: "Test Note",
    content: "Test content",
    createdAt: new Date(),
  };

  const mockOnPress = jest.fn();

  it("renders note title and content", () => {
    render(<NoteItem note={mockNote} onPress={mockOnPress} />);

    expect(screen.getByText("Test Note")).toBeTruthy();
    expect(screen.getByText("Test content")).toBeTruthy();
  });

  it("calls onPress when pressed", () => {
    render(<NoteItem note={mockNote} onPress={mockOnPress} />);

    fireEvent.press(screen.getByText("Test Note"));
    expect(mockOnPress).toHaveBeenCalledWith("1");
  });

  it("handles empty content gracefully", () => {
    const emptyNote = { ...mockNote, content: "" };
    render(<NoteItem note={emptyNote} onPress={mockOnPress} />);

    expect(screen.getByText("Test Note")).toBeTruthy();
    expect(screen.queryByText("Test content")).toBeNull();
  });
});
```

### Mocking Guidelines

- **Mock API calls** with jest.mock()
- **Mock navigation** functions for route testing
- **Mock external libraries** that don't work in test environment
- **Use mock data** that represents real data structure

### Test Coverage

- **Aim for high coverage** on business logic
- **Test edge cases** and error scenarios
- **Test user interactions** thoroughly
- **Test accessibility** features

### Running Tests

- **`yarn test`**: Run tests in watch mode
- **`yarn test --coverage`**: Run tests with coverage report
- **`yarn test --watchAll=false`**: Run tests once
